{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IndexingIterator","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Elements","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Elements","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection","text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"text":" type is the default iterator for any collection that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t declare its own. It acts as an iterator by using a collection’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices to step over each value in the collection. Most collections in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard library use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" as their iterator."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, any custom collection type you create will inherit a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeIterator()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method that returns an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IndexingIterator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"making it unnecessary to declare your own. When creating a custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection type, add the minimal requirements of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Collection"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol: starting and ending indices and a subscript for accessing","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. With those elements defined, the inherited "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"method satisfies the requirements of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s an example of a type that declares the minimal requirements for a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" structure is a fixed-size collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that always holds two elements of a specific type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct CollectionOfTwo<Element>: Collection {","    let elements: (Element, Element)","","    init(_ first: Element, _ second: Element) {","        self.elements = (first, second)","    }","","    var startIndex: Int { return 0 }","    var endIndex: Int   { return 2 }","","    subscript(index: Int) -> Element {","        switch index {","        case 0: return elements.0","        case 1: return elements.1","        default: fatalError(\"Index out of bounds.\")","        }","    }","    ","    func index(after i: Int) -> Int {","        precondition(i < endIndex, \"Can't advance beyond endIndex\")","        return i + 1","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t define its own "},{"code":"makeIterator()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Iterator"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type, it uses the default iterator type,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"IndexingIterator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This example shows how a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CollectionOfTwo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"can be created holding the values of a point, and then iterated over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using a "},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-","type":"text"},{"code":"in","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let point = CollectionOfTwo(15.0, 20.0)","for element in point {","    print(element)","}","\/\/ Prints \"15.0\"","\/\/ Prints \"20.0\""]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorProtocol","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sequence"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"title":"IndexingIterator","externalID":"s:s16IndexingIteratorV","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"10.10"},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text